    {
      "title": "Evaluate a fresh action for actor improvement",
      "explanation": "For the policy objective, replay supplies the state $s_O$. The current actor samples $a_\\pi=f_\\phi(\\epsilon;s_O)$ and provides $\\log\\pi_\\phi(a_\\pi\\mid s_O)$. Both critics evaluate $(s_O,a_\\pi)$, producing $Q_{1\\pi}$ and $Q_{2\\pi}$; their minimum is $Q_{\\min\\pi}=\\min_i Q_{\\theta_i}(s_O,a_\\pi)$. Actor improvement uses this fresh-action minimum, not the stored-action estimates.",
